Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Special conformal symmetry Ward identities", "Chapter",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Gill Sans MT",
 FontSize->20,
 FontWeight->"Bold",
 FontSlant->"Italic",
 FontColor->RGBColor[0.5, 0, 0.5]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The six independent projections follow Table 1 and Eqs. (15)-(16) of the \
article. The projected coefficients retain the normalization of the \
calculation: the common factor phi is removed for vertices with an odd number \
of field legs. Left expressions are dimensional contributions and right \
expressions are loop contributions. Conformal invariance requires ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["C", "L"], TraditionalForm]]],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["C", "R"], TraditionalForm]]],
 "; their difference measures the violation at finite truncation order."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0020581485220985`*^9, 4.0020581562123876`*^9}},
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Gill Sans MT",
 FontSize->14],

Cell["\<\
In each right-hand contribution, the scale derivative of R and the momentum \
integration are displayed explicitly. The regulator derivative is shown as a \
common factor multiplying each conformal loop kernel; the fixed-point \
integrands above already contain this factor.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.002060177202701*^9, 4.002060178683468*^9}},
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Gill Sans MT",
 FontSize->14],

